  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great Apes Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to maintain the habitats of the yellow-cheeked crested gibbon within the Bu Gia Map National Park by changing local peoples attitudes regarding wildfire prevention and suppression. This will be done by: 1. continuing to improve the relationships between communities and forest rangers as a way to prevent wildfire in Bu Gia Map National Park; 2. training at least 50% of local people to effectively manage fire inside the parks forests; 3. training at least eighty percent of the households residing near the parks forests to understand the risk of wildfire and how to suppress fires; 4. regularly monitoring the most flammable sites in the park to prevent wildfire during the dry season; 5. and equipping the most flammable areas in the park with signboards to help local people prevent wildfires.</narrative>
  </description>
